              "text": "Let the second field produce 120 tons.\n\n- First field: \"2.5 times more than the second\" typically means 2.5 × 120 = 300 tons.\n- Third field: \"40% less than the first\" means 60% of the first: 0.60 × 300 = 180 tons.\n\nTotal production = 120 + 300 + 180 = 600 tons.\n\nAnswer: 600 tons. (Note: “2.5 times more” is commonly interpreted as “2.5 times as much.”)",
